      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Vintage ; :hasLegalityStatus :Legal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pioneer ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pauper ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ;
    :hasRuling
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2023-04-14"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """To determine the number of differently named artifact tokens you control, count each artifact token you control once, but only if its English name isn’t exactly the same as another artifact token you’ve already counted this way."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2023-04-14"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """A token’s name is its subtypes plus the word “Token” unless it’s copying another object or it was given a specific name by the effect that created it. For example, the tokens created by Gimbal’s last ability are named “Gremlin Token.” These tokens have the same name as the 2/2 red Gremlin creature tokens created by Release the Gremlins."""@en ] .

:GlimmervoidBasin rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  :Card ;
    :cardName "Glimmervoid Basin" ;
    :manaValue "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    :hasCardType :Plane ;
    :hasSubType :Mirrodin ;
    :hasRarity :Common ;
    :isInSet :MarchOfTheMachineCommander ;
    :cardNumber "143"^^xsd:integer ;
    :artist "Lars Grant-West" ;
    :hasLanguage :English ;
    :printedText """Whenever a player casts an instant or sorcery spell with a single target, that player copies that spell for each other spell, permanent, card not on the battlefield, and/or player the spell could target. Each copy targets a different one of them.
Whenever chaos ensues, choose target creature. Each player except that creature's controller creates a token that's a copy of that creature."""@en ;
    :oracleText """Whenever a player casts an instant or sorcery spell with a single target, that player copies that spell for each other spell, permanent, card not on the battlefield, and/or player the spell could target. Each copy targets a different one of them.
Whenever chaos ensues, choose target creature. Each player except that creature's controller creates a token that's a copy of that creature."""@en ;
    :gathererUrl "https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=615134"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :scryfallUrl "https://scryfall.com/card/moc/143/glimmervoid-basin"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :hasLegality
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Commander ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Standard ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Modern ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Legacy ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Vintage ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pioneer ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pauper ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ;
    :hasRuling
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Anything that couldn't be targeted by the original spell (due to shroud, protection abilities, targeting restrictions, or any other reason) is just ignored by Glimmervoid Basin's first ability."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """A face-up plane card that's turned face down becomes a new object with no relation to its previous existence. In particular, it loses all counters it may have had."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """Other than choices involving modes or additional costs, the copies are created based on what they could target if the spell were cast anew. For example, if a player casts Naturalize ("Destroy target artifact or enchantment") targeting an artifact, Glimmervoid Basin's first ability will copy it for each artifact and enchantment it could target (and each copy will target a different one of those), not just for each artifact it could target."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The controller of a face-up plane card is the player designated as the "planar controller." Normally, the planar controller is whoever the active player is. However, if the current planar controller would leave the game, instead the next player in turn order that wouldn't leave the game becomes the planar controller, then the old planar controller leaves the game. The new planar controller retains that designation until they leave the game or a different player becomes the active player, whichever comes first."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """A plane card is treated as if its text box included "When you roll {PW}, put this card on the bottom of its owner's planar deck face down, then move the top card of your planar deck off that planar deck and turn it face up." This is called the "planeswalking ability.\""""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If the spell that's copied has an X whose value was determined as it was cast (like Earthquake does), the copy has the same value of X."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """As a token is created by the chaos ability, it checks the printed values of the creature it's copying, as well as any copy effects that have been applied to it. It won't copy counters on the creature, nor will it copy other effects that have changed the creature's power, toughness, types, color, and so on."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The controller of a copy can't choose to pay any additional costs for the copy. However, effects based on any additional costs that were paid for the original spell are copied as though those same costs were paid for the copy too."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If a spell targets multiple things, it won't cause Glimmervoid Basin's first ability to trigger, even if all but one of those targets has become illegal."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The copies that Glimmervoid Basin's first ability creates are created on the stack, so they're not "cast." Abilities that trigger when a player casts a spell (like Glimmervoid Basin's first ability itself) won't trigger."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The controller of the spell that caused Glimmervoid Basin's first ability to trigger also controls all the copies. That player chooses the order the copies are put onto the stack. The original spell will be on the stack beneath those copies and resolves last."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If a spell targets the same player or object multiple times, it won't cause Glimmervoid Basin's first ability to trigger."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If the spell that's copied is modal (that is, it says "Choose one —" or the like), the copy will have the same mode. Its controller can't choose a different one."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If an ability of a plane refers to "you," it's referring to whoever the plane's controller is at the time, not to the player that started the game with that plane card in their deck. Many abilities of plane cards affect all players, while many others affect only the planar controller, so read each ability carefully."""@en ] .

:IsleOfVesuva rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                  :Card ;
    :cardName "Isle of Vesuva" ;
    :manaValue "0"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    :hasCardType :Plane ;
    :hasSubType :Dominaria ;
    :hasRarity :Common ;
    :isInSet :MarchOfTheMachineCommander ;
    :cardNumber "147"^^xsd:integer ;
    :artist "Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai" ;
    :hasLanguage :English ;
    :printedText """Whenever a nontoken creature enters, its controller creates a token that's a copy of that creature.
Whenever chaos ensues, destroy target creature and all other creatures with the same name as that creature."""@en ;
    :oracleText """Whenever a nontoken creature enters, its controller creates a token that's a copy of that creature.
Whenever chaos ensues, destroy target creature and all other creatures with the same name as that creature."""@en ;
    :gathererUrl "https://gatherer.wizards.com/Pages/Card/Details.aspx?multiverseid=615138"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :scryfallUrl "https://scryfall.com/card/moc/147/isle-of-vesuva"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    :hasLegality
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Commander ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Standard ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Modern ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Legacy ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Vintage ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pioneer ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ,
      [ rdf:type :LegalityMapping ; :inFormat :Pauper ; :hasLegalityStatus :NotLegal ] ;
    :hasRuling
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """As a token is created by Isle of Vesuva's first ability, it checks the printed values of the creature it's copying, as well as any copy effects that have been applied to it. It won't copy counters on the creature, nor will it copy other effects that have changed the creature's power, toughness, types, color, and so on."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The chaos ability will destroy all creatures with the same name as the target creature, not just tokens created by Isle of Vesuva's first ability. It doesn't matter who controls them."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """The controller of a face-up plane card is the player designated as the "planar controller." Normally, the planar controller is whoever the active player is. However, if the current planar controller would leave the game, instead the next player in turn order that wouldn't leave the game becomes the planar controller, then the old planar controller leaves the game. The new planar controller retains that designation until they leave the game or a different player becomes the active player, whichever comes first."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """A face-up plane card that's turned face down becomes a new object with no relation to its previous existence. In particular, it loses all counters it may have had."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """A plane card is treated as if its text box included "When you roll {PW}, put this card on the bottom of its owner's planar deck face down, then move the top card of your planar deck off that planar deck and turn it face up." This is called the "planeswalking ability.\""""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """A face-down creature has no name, so it doesn't have the same name as anything else."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If the permanent targeted by the chaos ability has become an illegal target by the time the ability resolves, the ability doesn't resolve. Nothing will be destroyed."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If an ability of a plane refers to "you," it's referring to whoever the plane's controller is at the time, not to the player that started the game with that plane card in their deck. Many abilities of plane cards affect all players, while many others affect only the planar controller, so read each ability carefully."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If the creature that caused Isle of Vesuva's first ability to trigger has already left the battlefield by the time the ability resolves, the ability still creates a token. It will have the copiable values of the characteristics of that nontoken creature as it last existed on the battlefield."""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2009-10-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """A token's name is the same as the creature types listed by the effect that created it, unless the token copies a permanent or that effect specifically gives that token a name. For example, the effect of The Fourth Sphere's chaos ability creates a token with the name "Zombie.\""""@en ] ,
      [ rdf:type :Ruling ;
        :rulingDate "2013-07-01"^^xsd:date ;
        :rulingText """If the permanent targeted by the chaos ability isn't destroyed (because it regenerates, or because it has indestructible), all other permanents with the same name as it will still be destroyed."""@en ] .

